  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 345 AM CDT Thu May 14 2026\n\nNear term (remainder of the week into the weekend): In the wake of\nthe recent surface cold frontal passage, sunny skies will lead to\nwell-mixed conditions and low afternoon humidity. Then as we go \nbeyond today, a weather pattern change is expected with the mean \nsubtropical ridge axis shifting from the Southern Plains to the \nsouth Atlantic coast. While it will remain rain-free, the \nresulting shift from northerly to southerly low level winds will \nincrease the humidity quite a bit.\n\nLonger term (early to mid next week): Continued moisture transport\nwill support an increase in diurnally enhanced shower and\nthunderstorm chances, especially over western and northern\nportions of the area where there will be greater potential for at\nleast minor height falls/ascent to interact with the greater\nmoisture. Along with the increasing rain chances, temperatures\nwill be on the increase with lower 90s becoming more common. The\nabove normal temperatures combined with increasing humidity will \nlikely result in heat index values in the mid/upper 90s. /EC/",
